Documentation priority

Before any public pilot: privacy notice, full DPIA, DPAs, vendor/transfer register, no-training terms, consent/cookie configuration, access controls, automated deletion, and rights workflow.

Before processing the first real user: perform an end-to-end test using synthetic data, including access export, correction, withdrawal, deletion across all processors, backup expiry, and incident escalation.

During operation: keep a ROPA, rights/request log, deletion evidence, breach register, vendor change log, DPIA review record, and periodic access review.

Accountability conclusion

The written analysis is now substantially stronger, but a regulator would ask for operational evidence rather than policy statements alone. MIRA is therefore documented enough for a controlled synthetic-data prototype, not ready for uncontrolled real-user deployment.
